Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: xx/xx/2024]
1.  Measured resonances: from Endt 1998, Chronidou et al. 1999, Harissopulos et al. 2000; these were normalized to our standard strengths for Elab = 632 and 992 keV;
    resonances at Er < 500 keV: Endt 1998 was disregarded and the values of Harissopulos et al. 2000 were normalized to our standard strength for Elab = 406 keV. 
2.  Er = 73 keV [Ex = 11657 keV]: partial widths estimated from measured Gp [transfer], (a,g) strength, and Ga/G; Gp is obtained from the upper limit on the weak
    ell=0 component and the lower limit provided by the dominant ell=2 component of the transfer angular distribution. 
3.  Er = 86 keV [Ex = 11670 keV]: only an upper limit can be obtained from proton transfer for Gp; Gg and Ga are derived from the measured (a,g) strength and Ga/G. 
4.  Er = 195.07 keV [Ex = 11778.7 keV; 2+]: Gp and Gg are estimated from shell-model results; Ga is derived from the measured (a,g) strength, which belongs to this,
    natural parity, component of the doublet. The derived (p,g) strength is much smaller (factor 20) than the measured value for the doublet and, thus, the latter
    most likely belongs to the 5+ component.
5.  Er = 196.27 keV [Ex = 11778.9 keV; 5+]: Gp is derived from the measured (p,g) strength of the doublet [see previous comment]; Gg is adopted from the shell model.   
6.  ENSDF 2013 lists a third level, at 11780.7 (0+ - 4+); we find no compelling evidence that this state is distinct from Ex = 11778.7 keV (2+). 
7.  Er = 350 keV [Ex = 11933 keV; 5+]: Gp estimated from shell model; Gg = 1 eV is an approximate estimate based on shell-model results for neighboring states.
8.  Er = 402 keV [Ex= 11986 keV; 1+]: Gp upper limit from measured proton transfer spectrum; Gg = 1 eV is an approximate estimate based on shell-model results for 
    neighboring states.
9.  Er = 439 keV [Ex = 12023 keV; 5-]: Gp upper limit from measured proton transfer spectrum; Gg = 1 eV is an approximate estimate based on shell-model results for 
    neighboring states.
10. Direct capture S factor estimated using experimental C2S from Endt 1977, Endt 1990, Vernotte et al. 1994.
